1
00:00:01,040 --> 00:00:03,240
Cinderella

2
00:00:06,290 --> 00:00:11,930
Cinderella's Sister

3
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:21,180
Cinderella's Sister

4
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:24,060
Episode 6

5
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:30,480
This is Kyung Wha Chung.

6
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:35,100
Don't you remember anything?

7
00:00:59,740 --> 00:01:01,800
You're so simple...

8
00:01:02,890 --> 00:01:08,170
Can you just forget it all if you choose to?

9
00:02:07,580 --> 00:02:10,230
Do you really not have anything to say to me?

10
00:02:28,610 --> 00:02:31,190
Let go!

11
00:02:32,470 --> 00:02:34,430
Let go of me! Let go!

12
00:02:48,310 --> 00:02:50,220
Eun Jo.

13
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:01,830
Eun Jo...

14
00:03:08,310 --> 00:03:10,380
Eun Jo.

15
00:03:35,380 --> 00:03:39,620
Whoever you were, how you smiled, or what your name was.

16
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:42,790
None of that matters now.

17
00:03:42,790 --> 00:03:47,950
You're nothing more than a bug or mote of dust to me.

18
00:03:47,950 --> 00:03:51,690
Calling my name and smiling at me.

19
00:03:51,690 --> 00:03:58,830
I dare you to do it. Then really, I'll just kill you.

20
00:04:53,660 --> 00:04:57,820
Son, did you have a bad dream?

21
00:04:57,820 --> 00:05:01,400
It was just a dream so don't cry, my son.

22
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:04,290
This horrible punk.

23
00:05:04,290 --> 00:05:06,320
You little punk.

24
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:08,530
This adorable, horrible punk.

25
00:05:08,530 --> 00:05:11,390
This little, little, adorable punk.

26
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:18,790
My son.

27
00:05:19,680 --> 00:05:23,620
Everyone went on a picnic

28
00:05:33,690 --> 00:05:36,130
without me.

29
00:05:42,720 --> 00:05:45,200
Without me.

30
00:05:51,730 --> 00:05:54,210
Without me.

31
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:19,340
What is it?

32
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:24,630
You can leave now.

33
00:06:26,150 --> 00:06:31,990
There are lots of others who can do research on yeast.

34
00:06:33,910 --> 00:06:40,040
I didn't think you were staying around with a plan to leave.

35
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:47,260
You were clear and brave. Not only was your brain fast but so is your feet.

36
00:06:47,260 --> 00:06:51,430
If you want to fly,

37
00:06:51,430 --> 00:06:55,790
I plan on giving you wings.

38
00:06:55,790 --> 00:06:57,410
I've never thought

39
00:06:57,410 --> 00:07:03,700
that you had to ever say anything bad to me, not once.

40
00:07:05,330 --> 00:07:07,190
I know.

41
00:07:07,190 --> 00:07:09,520
You know?

42
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:11,190
Yes.

43
00:07:12,090 --> 00:07:14,660
You don't know that. You don't.

44
00:07:14,660 --> 00:07:18,680
If you knew, you wouldn't have thought of a plan like that.

45
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:25,370
I've never thought of you as different from Hyo Seon.
(as his daughter)

46
00:07:29,820 --> 00:07:33,560
Well, I guess there may have been times.

47
00:07:33,560 --> 00:07:36,240
But that's in my subconsciousness,

48
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:42,220
that I neither am aware of nor want to know.

49
00:07:42,220 --> 00:07:46,350
Even if you say I've hidden away something like that in my subconscioues,

50
00:07:46,350 --> 00:07:51,030
I wouldn't think that of you.

51
00:07:54,530 --> 00:07:58,340
I thought you thought of me the same way.

52
00:08:01,070 --> 00:08:04,060
Give me your plans.

53
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:10,050
I... have the right to know at least that much.

54
00:08:12,050 --> 00:08:14,760
If you've been here only for the purpose of paying back a debt,

55
00:08:14,760 --> 00:08:18,580
you must have had other thoughts in your mind.

56
00:08:18,580 --> 00:08:22,190
Things you've wanted to do, how much you've prepared,

57
00:08:22,190 --> 00:08:25,190
or how you're going to live out in the world.

58
00:08:25,190 --> 00:08:30,420
At the very least, since I've changed your surname from your mom's to mine,

59
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:35,450
and I've been the guardian of a child named Goo Eun Jo,

60
00:08:35,450 --> 00:08:39,610
I deserve to know your plans for the future.

61
00:08:43,790 --> 00:08:46,020
I'll give it to you.

62
00:08:47,210 --> 00:08:49,130
My plans.

63
00:08:51,450 --> 00:08:55,560
Okay. You can leave now.

64
00:09:07,700 --> 00:09:10,850
Are you letting Eun Jo leave?

65
00:09:10,850 --> 00:09:14,430
Let's talk about this later.

66
00:09:16,380 --> 00:09:19,630
Are you leaving?

67
00:09:24,960 --> 00:09:29,800
Are you chasing us out?

68
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:34,820
Wh-What are you talking about?

69
00:09:34,820 --> 00:09:40,220
Are you chasing me and Eun Jo out right now?

70
00:09:44,290 --> 00:09:45,990
Honey,

71
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:51,760
I didn't think something like this would happen again.

72
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:54,860
If I did something wrong, forgive me!

73
00:09:57,260 --> 00:10:02,330
Darling, I must not have satisfied you with all my shortcomings.

74
00:10:02,330 --> 00:10:06,210
But still... I really gave it my all.

75
00:10:06,210 --> 00:10:11,530
I don't even know what's good, but tried to be good no matter what.

76
00:10:11,530 --> 00:10:12,770
Honey!

77
00:10:12,770 --> 00:10:14,420
Seriously...

78
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:17,570
Honey, Honey!

79
00:10:17,570 --> 00:10:20,090
Honey! Listen. Why are you being like this?

80
00:10:20,090 --> 00:10:23,560
Listen to me!

81
00:10:25,390 --> 00:10:26,570
Mom!

82
00:10:26,570 --> 00:10:27,550
Honey!

83
00:10:27,550 --> 00:10:29,140
Mom!

84
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:34,440
What?

85
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:36,800
I said let's get married.

86
00:10:39,310 --> 00:10:44,510
I've decided on that, so you should decide on that, too.

87
00:10:44,510 --> 00:10:46,650
Decide on what?

88
00:10:46,650 --> 00:10:51,110
To marry me.

89
00:10:51,110 --> 00:10:54,020
Okay, sure.

90
00:10:55,030 --> 00:10:59,980
No matter how much you like Eun Jo, I won't allow it.

91
00:11:02,830 --> 00:11:06,330
If even you go to Eun Jo, what will I have left?

92
00:11:06,330 --> 00:11:08,190
Hyo Seon...

93
00:11:14,420 --> 00:11:17,020
You're mine.

94
00:11:17,020 --> 00:11:22,700
Since you've agreed to be mine, don't change your mind.

95
00:11:35,020 --> 00:11:38,070
Doctor, is she going to be okay?

96
00:11:38,070 --> 00:11:40,470
You don't have to worry, she'll be fine.

97
00:11:40,470 --> 00:11:43,380
- Come this way, I'll see you off.
- Alright.

98
00:12:09,870 --> 00:12:12,080
Where's Joon Soo?

99
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:15,860
Are you okay?

100
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:19,420
Joon Soo is at Ichon, don't worry.

101
00:12:19,420 --> 00:12:22,150
Where's your father?

102
00:12:22,150 --> 00:12:25,390
He's escorting Hyo Seon's grandfather home.

103
00:12:26,150 --> 00:12:30,110
Don't say anything. You're weak right now.

104
00:12:30,110 --> 00:12:35,200
Outside... is anyone there?

105
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:37,270
No one is there.

106
00:12:39,380 --> 00:12:41,820
I said don't speak.

107
00:12:43,290 --> 00:12:45,730
You bitch. You crazy bitch!

108
00:12:45,730 --> 00:12:48,020
Why would you leave?

109
00:12:48,020 --> 00:12:51,750
If you just stay like this, the factory, the house, and the company

110
00:12:51,750 --> 00:12:53,740
could become entirely yours and Joon Soo's.

111
00:12:53,740 --> 00:12:57,350
What nonsense are you speaking, talking about leaving?

112
00:12:57,350 --> 00:12:59,040
I was relieved

113
00:12:59,040 --> 00:13:02,170
because I thought you understood what you had to do.

114
00:13:02,170 --> 00:13:04,720
But what? Leave?

115
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:09,580
So...

116
00:13:11,180 --> 00:13:13,510
you put on a show?

117
00:13:14,730 --> 00:13:18,380
It's weird to take back something you've already said,

118
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:20,920
so just say you can't leave seeing how uneasy it makes my mother.

119
00:13:20,920 --> 00:13:24,120
Use me as your excuse, okay?

120
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:28,350
I can't do this. Get me some water.

121
00:13:29,110 --> 00:13:30,630
I'm not like before.

122
00:13:30,630 --> 00:13:34,490
If I act like I'm fainting, I'll faint for real!

123
00:13:38,260 --> 00:13:40,360
I should've just...

124
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:44,210
What? What are you saying?

125
00:13:44,210 --> 00:13:48,480
I should've just died.

126
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:50,250
What?

127
00:13:51,440 --> 00:13:54,390
I had so many opportunities to die.

128
00:13:56,670 --> 00:14:01,860
There were so many opportunities

129
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:05,380
for me to not be involved with you.

130
00:14:05,380 --> 00:14:08,220
What are you murmuring?

131
00:14:08,220 --> 00:14:11,940
Omo...am I hearing things?

132
00:14:16,370 --> 00:14:18,580
You just try saying something like that again.

133
00:14:18,580 --> 00:14:21,670
Then, I'll really show you things you shouldn't see.

134
00:14:21,670 --> 00:14:22,800
Go get me ice water!

135
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:25,000
Mom!

136
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:29,530
Mom!

137
00:14:36,810 --> 00:14:38,780
Mom!

138
00:14:43,990 --> 00:14:46,030
I'm okay.

139
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:30,860
Did I not hear something?

140
00:17:31,640 --> 00:17:33,260
What?

141
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:35,820
Did you say something to me?

142
00:17:37,720 --> 00:17:39,780
Are you here on an errand?

143
00:17:39,780 --> 00:17:42,570
It's not an errand...

144
00:17:42,570 --> 00:17:47,100
Then is the chairman looking for me?

145
00:17:52,660 --> 00:17:55,370
Tell him I'll be there in the afternoon.

146
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:03,740
Noona.

147
00:18:22,460 --> 00:18:25,490
You haven't told anyone about this, have you?

148
00:18:25,490 --> 00:18:27,410
No.

149
00:18:34,750 --> 00:18:37,000
I'm scared that someone's going to see this.

150
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:41,380
Even if you're upset by it, it's better than nothing.

151
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:47,960
Are you already paying me my salary?

152
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:50,680
It's not your salary.

153
00:18:53,650 --> 00:18:56,650
There's just something like that.

154
00:18:58,240 --> 00:19:01,270
Don't be curious about it!

155
00:19:26,950 --> 00:19:29,080
Mom!

156
00:19:29,080 --> 00:19:31,430
Joon Soo, mom's right here.

157
00:19:34,220 --> 00:19:36,860
Mom! My toy gun!

158
00:19:36,860 --> 00:19:38,130
Okay, I'll give you your toy.

159
00:19:38,130 --> 00:19:42,530
♫  I feel I can reach you if I extend my hand ♫

160
00:19:44,670 --> 00:19:48,970
♫  I see you in front of me ♫

161
00:19:50,990 --> 00:19:56,940
♫ "Don't go", I cannot say those words yet ♫

162
00:19:56,940 --> 00:20:03,360
♫  I must be standing here just looking toward you ♫

163
00:20:03,360 --> 00:20:09,620
♫  Turn around please, Turn yourself around again please ♫

164
00:20:09,620 --> 00:20:15,410
♫  If you go away like this, can you really live without me?  ♫

165
00:20:15,410 --> 00:20:22,840
♫  You cannot go because I won't live even a day  ♫

166
00:20:22,860 --> 00:20:33,000
♫  I'm still standing here staring at you  ♫

167
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:38,650
Don't you love yeast?

168
00:20:38,650 --> 00:20:44,210
I like yeast the most in the world. I like it a hundred, a thousand times more than my husband.

169
00:20:44,210 --> 00:20:48,640
Yeast doesn't play poker or cheat.

170
00:20:50,940 --> 00:20:54,560
Please save me, little guys.

171
00:20:55,570 --> 00:20:58,220
By the way, do you want to go on a blind date?

172
00:20:58,220 --> 00:21:03,750
He's a great man who, unlike mine, doesn't play poker as his hobby.

173
00:21:03,750 --> 00:21:05,800
I mentioned him to you last time.

174
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:09,440
I told him you didn't want to, so I declined once already,

175
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:14,360
but he won't give up and keeps asking. Huh?

176
00:21:20,010 --> 00:21:23,740
Dae Seong True Winemakers

177
00:21:29,350 --> 00:21:33,430
Until he finds a better place and walks out himself,

178
00:21:33,430 --> 00:21:39,120
I won't send Gi Hoon away.

179
00:21:40,420 --> 00:21:42,840
Gi Hoon is a pitiful child.

180
00:21:44,220 --> 00:21:50,460
The reason he worked so hard, all by himself, to study

181
00:21:50,460 --> 00:21:54,120
and came all the way here is because I'm here.

182
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:59,690
He came looking for my shadow because he was lonely.

183
00:22:02,340 --> 00:22:06,560
You're arrogant. Do you know that?

184
00:22:13,160 --> 00:22:15,650
Did you bring me your plan?

185
00:22:16,940 --> 00:22:18,580
No.

186
00:22:20,690 --> 00:22:24,760
Did you change your mind because of Mom?

187
00:22:29,820 --> 00:22:36,640
If you had actually written up a report like I told you to, and waved it in my face,

188
00:22:36,640 --> 00:22:40,810
I really don't know how I would've felt.

189
00:22:40,810 --> 00:22:42,820
Good on you for not writing one.

190
00:22:43,820 --> 00:22:50,070
I know that you're not one to starve to death, wherever you are.

191
00:22:51,260 --> 00:22:56,960
That's not what I meant when I said I wouldn't have to worry about you wherever you end up.

192
00:22:56,960 --> 00:23:02,720
I want you to find somewhere your heart is warm,

193
00:23:03,620 --> 00:23:07,550
where it can stay without flailing around.

194
00:23:07,550 --> 00:23:10,940
Until then, I want to take care of you.

195
00:23:12,550 --> 00:23:16,430
You speaking as if you would leave after you've paid back you 'debts' to me?

196
00:23:16,430 --> 00:23:19,900
It makes it clear you don't understand my intentions.

197
00:23:19,900 --> 00:23:23,790
It wasn't for many days,

198
00:23:23,790 --> 00:23:26,760
but my heart ached in misery after you said that.

199
00:23:28,550 --> 00:23:30,940
Don't do that again, okay?

200
00:23:32,750 --> 00:23:34,820
This house...

201
00:23:36,850 --> 00:23:38,920
is difficult for me.

202
00:23:41,050 --> 00:23:43,850
Don't give me affection.

203
00:23:45,200 --> 00:23:49,640
If you have, take it all back.

204
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:54,420
I'm a horrible person.

205
00:23:54,420 --> 00:23:59,050
You can't even imagine how wicked I am.

206
00:23:59,050 --> 00:24:05,010
If you knew the kind of thoughts I have while living,

207
00:24:05,010 --> 00:24:07,630
you wouldn't want to see me for even a second.

208
00:24:08,820 --> 00:24:14,420
For now, I've been stopped by Mom, but I will leave eventually,

209
00:24:14,420 --> 00:24:16,670
whether it be because I pay back my debts with my research or

210
00:24:16,670 --> 00:24:21,010
because I get married to the man I'm meeting on my blind date.

211
00:24:21,950 --> 00:24:23,460
So...

212
00:24:25,700 --> 00:24:28,360
don't take a liking to me.

213
00:24:28,360 --> 00:24:33,070
I'm not someone who will live in gratitude forever

214
00:24:33,070 --> 00:24:38,660
just because you give me some trust.

215
00:24:50,560 --> 00:24:51,630
What did you say?

216
00:24:51,630 --> 00:24:53,940
I'll help you in other ways.

217
00:24:53,940 --> 00:24:57,390
The work I'm doing right now doesn't

218
00:24:57,390 --> 00:25:00,870
permit me to analyze finances or accounting.

219
00:25:02,460 --> 00:25:06,390
Nor do I have a wish to have to approach those things if I don't need to.

220
00:25:06,390 --> 00:25:08,600
Why did you have your mind?

221
00:25:09,740 --> 00:25:14,160
Have you grown more fond of Goo Dae Sung-

222
00:25:14,160 --> 00:25:18,280
I've not the Hong Gi Hoon from 8 years ago.

223
00:25:18,280 --> 00:25:22,960
When I left that place, I threw my old self away.

224
00:25:22,960 --> 00:25:27,810
Maybe that would be the case if I had never left, but once I did, I forgot everything.

225
00:25:27,810 --> 00:25:30,860
Then why are you hesitating?

226
00:25:30,860 --> 00:25:35,220
What do you mean, you don't want to approach it if you don't need to?

227
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:47,000
It's kind of similar to princes in the Joseon Dynasty fighting over the throne. Isn't it?

228
00:25:47,890 --> 00:25:51,090
The son working to overthrow his father

229
00:25:51,090 --> 00:25:53,510
and his father wants to strike down his son.

230
00:25:53,510 --> 00:25:57,080
He gives his support to a hidden prince-

231
00:25:57,080 --> 00:26:00,310
And on top of that, the prince that is of that worth

232
00:26:00,310 --> 00:26:04,130
pounces on the person who took him in and ruins him.

233
00:26:04,130 --> 00:26:06,360
Shut up, you bastard!

234
00:26:07,230 --> 00:26:11,680
To use a sword to cut him up,

235
00:26:11,680 --> 00:26:14,420
but the opponent is too young.

236
00:26:14,420 --> 00:26:17,900
I'm ashamed of using a sword, so I put it away.

237
00:26:18,810 --> 00:26:22,260
Dae Sung isn't your opponent.

238
00:26:22,260 --> 00:26:24,180
You can ignore them.

239
00:26:24,180 --> 00:26:25,960
What would you know?

240
00:26:25,960 --> 00:26:29,680
I'm just resting there for a moment.

241
00:26:29,680 --> 00:26:33,010
As I rest, I'll think of ways I can help you.

242
00:26:33,010 --> 00:26:39,450
A way to double, triple, your strength without taking over Dae Sung.

243
00:26:39,450 --> 00:26:46,130
A way to save you and not have the company stolen by Gi Jeong.

244
00:26:48,020 --> 00:26:53,050
You say Dae Sung isn't our opponent?

245
00:26:54,280 --> 00:26:57,400
Do you think they are?

246
00:26:57,400 --> 00:26:59,930
You half-witted punk.

247
00:27:04,700 --> 00:27:06,800
What is this?

248
00:27:07,650 --> 00:27:09,420
Look at it.

249
00:27:16,400 --> 00:27:22,690
It's a report of the number of times Gi Jeong has tried to purchase Dae Sung Co.

250
00:27:23,560 --> 00:27:28,250
He's failed. Goo Dae Seong didn't put it up for sale.

251
00:27:29,130 --> 00:27:33,330
Gi Jeong... isn't giving up.

252
00:27:33,330 --> 00:27:37,680
I can't just let Gi Jeong purchase it.

253
00:27:42,350 --> 00:27:45,450
Shall I tell you one more thing?

254
00:27:47,800 --> 00:27:50,000
Do you know...

255
00:27:53,490 --> 00:27:56,200
how your mother died?

256
00:28:36,250 --> 00:28:40,920
My father is the chief surgeon at Myeongjin Hospital.

257
00:28:40,920 --> 00:28:45,530
My mother is a professor in the design department of Seonhwa University.

258
00:28:45,530 --> 00:28:49,300
My older brother is a prosecutor at the Seoul Metropolitan Prosecutor's Office,

259
00:28:49,300 --> 00:28:52,690
and my younger sister is graduating from medical school this year.

260
00:28:53,450 --> 00:28:57,190
I heard you weren't interested in anything about it.

261
00:28:57,190 --> 00:29:01,800
To be honest, I was really curious about you, so I asked a lot of questions.

262
00:29:01,800 --> 00:29:02,500
Is that so?

263
00:29:02,500 --> 00:29:05,670
I was so shocked when I heard about you.

264
00:29:05,670 --> 00:29:06,440
Why?

265
00:29:06,440 --> 00:29:11,070
I heard you were the daughter of a rice wine company that is threatening Hong Joo Co.

266
00:29:11,070 --> 00:29:13,490
Since Hong Joo is such a large company,

267
00:29:13,490 --> 00:29:18,950
and Dae Sung Co was only known within the Daegu region up until just a few years ago.

268
00:29:18,950 --> 00:29:21,620
I was surprised at the speed at which it's been growing.

269
00:29:21,620 --> 00:29:27,360
I heard that Hong Joo is quite on edge these days, especially given they though Daeseong's growth was insignificant before?

270
00:29:27,360 --> 00:29:30,120
Is that what you were curious about me?

271
00:29:31,920 --> 00:29:35,550
How tall are you? 160 cm? 161cm?

272
00:29:35,550 --> 00:29:38,270
How tall do I have to be for you to marry me?

273
00:29:38,270 --> 00:29:41,220
- What?
- I'm asking how tall I have to be for you to marry me.

274
00:29:41,220 --> 00:29:44,600
170cm? 171cm?

275
00:29:44,600 --> 00:29:50,160
Why are you being like that? Do you have a complex about your height?

276
00:29:50,160 --> 00:29:53,100
I don't care about such things.

277
00:29:53,100 --> 00:29:56,690
If I were going to marry based on height, I should've met a model.

278
00:29:56,690 --> 00:29:59,530
I wouldn't have asked to meet you.

279
00:30:00,320 --> 00:30:05,950
Shouldn't you already have matured past the age of having a complex about something like your height?

280
00:30:06,920 --> 00:30:09,890
You look about 165cm with your heels on.

281
00:30:09,890 --> 00:30:14,430
That's enough for me. Showing off your inferiority complex like that isn't good!

282
00:30:14,430 --> 00:30:16,410
Excuse me!

283
00:30:22,020 --> 00:30:24,220
You're going on blind dates?

284
00:30:27,420 --> 00:30:30,130
I guess you don't like him.

285
00:30:30,130 --> 00:30:32,810
Judging from how quickly you left.

286
00:31:20,420 --> 00:31:21,270
Hello?

287
00:31:21,270 --> 00:31:24,410
Are you crazy? Slow down!

288
00:32:06,650 --> 00:32:08,170
Slow down.

289
00:32:08,170 --> 00:32:13,760
Drive slowly. I won't follow you. I'll go in front of you, come slowly.

290
00:32:13,760 --> 00:32:18,630
The road winds a lot. A lot of accidents happen. Something bad could happen!

291
00:32:19,610 --> 00:32:21,510
I won't chase you.

292
00:32:21,510 --> 00:32:25,430
I won't try to hold on, and I won't ask for you to hold on to me.

293
00:32:25,430 --> 00:32:28,650
So you don't have to try with all your might to escape to anywhere possible.

294
00:32:28,650 --> 00:32:30,390
Okay?

295
00:32:31,700 --> 00:32:34,580
I already...

296
00:33:13,780 --> 00:33:17,120
Do you have something to say to me?

297
00:33:44,100 --> 00:33:46,900
I'm only saluting someone who has fed me.

298
00:33:46,900 --> 00:33:48,700
Salute, ma'am.

299
00:34:16,790 --> 00:34:19,040
Calling...

300
00:34:28,240 --> 00:34:30,950
Just promise me one thing.

301
00:34:32,260 --> 00:34:35,090
If you take over Daeseong Co,

302
00:34:35,860 --> 00:34:38,360
give it to me right away.

303
00:34:39,510 --> 00:34:41,850
If you promise that,

304
00:34:44,130 --> 00:34:46,560
I'll start working.

305
00:35:07,800 --> 00:35:12,200
Why is our precious baby sitting here doing dirty work like this?

306
00:35:12,200 --> 00:35:13,370
Go inside!

307
00:35:13,370 --> 00:35:17,520
No, Granny. I have to do this. I can do well.

308
00:35:17,520 --> 00:35:20,530
What do you mean, do it well. You're spilling half of it.

309
00:35:20,530 --> 00:35:22,410
I'm going to do it well.

310
00:35:22,410 --> 00:35:27,310
If they say to wash rice, I'll wash it. If they say to ferment the yeast, I'll ferment it.

311
00:35:27,310 --> 00:35:28,640
And ...

312
00:35:29,960 --> 00:35:32,260
I'm going to get married, too.

313
00:35:35,620 --> 00:35:40,240
Won't you do it properly? Do you know what kind of rice this is?

314
00:35:40,240 --> 00:35:44,040
This is rice grown without the tiniest bit of herbicides or chemicals.

315
00:35:44,040 --> 00:35:50,110
It's organic rice grown by catching bugs with human hands.

316
00:35:50,110 --> 00:35:54,450
Don't you dare spill a single grain. Do it properly!

317
00:35:54,450 --> 00:35:58,590
I am. I mean I will do it.

318
00:36:08,720 --> 00:36:11,360
Granny, am I useless?

319
00:36:11,360 --> 00:36:13,200
What?

320
00:36:16,440 --> 00:36:20,410
I'm going to do everything well.

321
00:36:20,410 --> 00:36:22,580
I can do well.

322
00:36:38,780 --> 00:36:42,890
Once you're done with that, come see me. I'll wait in your room.

323
00:36:47,120 --> 00:36:49,030
Salute.

324
00:37:08,140 --> 00:37:11,080
Shall I dance more for you?

325
00:37:11,080 --> 00:37:14,040
No. You can take it off now.

326
00:37:15,390 --> 00:37:18,220
What are you doing?

327
00:37:19,200 --> 00:37:21,120
You're pretty.

328
00:37:23,010 --> 00:37:27,840
You calling me pretty... it won't work anymore.

329
00:37:29,920 --> 00:37:33,620
You're a liar.

330
00:37:33,620 --> 00:37:36,060
I know you're just trying to make me feel happy by saying I'm pretty,

331
00:37:36,060 --> 00:37:39,180
to get me to do whatever you want me to do.

332
00:37:40,080 --> 00:37:42,320
I won't be tricked twice.

333
00:37:44,990 --> 00:37:46,990
I'm glad.

334
00:37:49,540 --> 00:37:53,800
Do you think I'll do whatever you tell me to do?

335
00:37:54,830 --> 00:37:56,550
Won't you?

336
00:37:56,550 --> 00:38:01,170
If not, tell me now. I thought you liked this.

337
00:38:01,870 --> 00:38:05,270
This isn't something I'll force someone who doesn't want to do it to do.

338
00:38:05,270 --> 00:38:09,180
If you won't do it, I can use money.

339
00:38:09,180 --> 00:38:11,330
Your father's money.

340
00:38:17,680 --> 00:38:19,120
You ...

341
00:38:21,760 --> 00:38:23,240
are so wicked.

342
00:38:23,240 --> 00:38:25,200
Are you not going to do it?

343
00:38:25,200 --> 00:38:27,760
You won't, right?

344
00:38:27,760 --> 00:38:29,760
Okay then.

345
00:38:32,050 --> 00:38:33,990
Hey!

346
00:39:42,260 --> 00:39:43,300
It's delicious.

347
00:39:43,300 --> 00:39:45,420
One more time.

348
00:39:46,220 --> 00:39:48,290
Again?

349
00:39:48,290 --> 00:39:51,330
We haven't even started.

350
00:39:52,620 --> 00:39:54,430
Okay.

351
00:41:11,180 --> 00:41:15,350
Auntie, can you give us some more meat?

352
00:41:16,280 --> 00:41:18,780
And another bottle of soju!

353
00:41:20,900 --> 00:41:23,710
Give us rice wine instead of the soju!

354
00:41:23,710 --> 00:41:26,700
Daeseong rice wine.

355
00:41:26,700 --> 00:41:29,920
Why are you ordering alcohol when you can't even drink?

356
00:41:29,920 --> 00:41:32,600
You drink all of it.

357
00:41:32,600 --> 00:41:35,440
Two bottles of Daeseong's rice wine!

358
00:41:35,440 --> 00:41:38,420
No, three bottles!

359
00:41:42,660 --> 00:41:45,600
I think we'd better put Daeseong's logo on aprons and menus,

360
00:41:45,600 --> 00:41:48,390
